  "final_message": "Your hunch holds, with one correction: the dip is in Q2 2024 only. Q2 2023 was about normal. Three ports explain more than the whole dip: **Brackwater, Fennick and Ivelholm**.\n\n**Overall TEU by quarter**\n\n| | Q1 | Q2 | Q3 | Q4 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 2023 | 14,050 | 13,036 | 14,802 | 11,312 |\n| 2024 | 12,991 | **9,622** | 13,290 | 12,029 |\n\nShipment counts and USD value follow the same pattern. Q2 2024 had 115 shipments, against about 150\u2013160 in nearby quarters.\n\n**The three ports in Q2 2024**\n\n| Port | Shipments (other 2024 quarters \u2192 Q2) | TEU (avg of other 2024 quarters \u2192 Q2) |\n|---|---|---|\n| Brackwater | 16\u201322 \u2192 **7** | ~1,700 \u2192 **466** |\n| Fennick | 17\u201323 \u2192 **4** | ~1,750 \u2192 **366** |\n| Ivelholm | 16\u201320 \u2192 **4** | ~1,780 \u2192 **375** |\n\n- **How much of the dip they explain:** together they fell about 4,000 TEU below their usual level. Overall Q2 2024 was only about 3,150 TEU below the other 2024 quarters. The other seven ports were about 900 TEU *above* their own average, which partly offset the loss.\n- **What it looks like:** these ports dropped to about 5 shipments a month in April, May and June, then went straight back to 15\u201325 a month in July. That looks like a three-month outage or a data feed gap, not a gradual decline.\n- **It affects every carrier type:** container, bulk and tanker all fall at these ports. That points to a port or reporting cause rather than a problem in one segment.\n\n**One more thing:** there is a smaller dip in Q4 2023 (11,312 TEU). It's spread across most ports, so it's a different, broad-based pattern.\n\nBefore reading this as a real drop in freight, it's worth checking whether something happened at those three ports in April\u2013June 2024, or whether their data is just incomplete. A sudden on/off change like this is often a reporting gap.\n\nI did this analysis in standalone Python and haven't changed `notebooks/explore.py`. I can add cells there for the port-by-quarter pivot and a monthly chart comparing the three ports with the rest.",
